#X obj 1100 305 expr if(lp\$1on==1 && lp\$1p>=lp\$1s+lp\$1L \, lp\$1s+fmod(lp\$1p+lp\$1f/max(lp\$1sr \, 1)-lp\$1s \, max(lp\$1L \, 1e-09)) \, -1);
#X obj 1100 330 moses 0;
#X text 20 770 pads: beat loop = 1/4 1/2 1 2 4 8 16 32 beats (latching: the lit pad again or SHIFT+pad exits \, another pad resizes). loop roll = 1/16 1/8 1/4 1/2 1 2 4 8 beats while held \, then the track carries on where it would have been. loops start on the beat grid (or the roll grid under 1 beat) so engaging never jumps;
#X text 1000 400 the wrap is done per sample by expr~. a beat loop also moves the phasor back into the loop (every 50 ms and on exit) so the track position stays in the loop and the next block plays on seamlessly. cue \, seek \, eject \, load or a mode change exit the loop;
#X obj 300 315 expr if(padmode\$1==3 \, -\$f1 \, \$f1);
#X obj 300 340 moses 0;
#X obj 300 365 * -1;
#X obj 300 390 t f f f;
